Subject: Allow factors in ggvis plot to keep same colour
Message-ID: <IMdMLxKfmwc.-S-eAzZVBQAJ@ggvis.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggvis/c/IMdMLxKfmwc/m/-S-eAzZVBQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I've found ggvis to be a fantastic tool, but one of the problems I've encountered is when I use the factors in a column to dynamically add items from a checkbox, the colours of the different factors change as I add or remove them. Does anyone know of a way to set the colour for each factor?

    data %>%
        ggvis(x = input_select(objects.to.plot, map = as.name <http://as.name>, label = "X Axis"),
              y = input_select(objects.to.plot, map = as.name <http://as.name>, label = "Y Axis")) %>%

    layer_points(prop("fill", as.name <http://as.name>(input_factor)), size := input_slider(10, 100, label = "Point Size"),
                     opacity := input_slider(0, 1, label = "Opacity")) %>%

    scale_ordinal("stroke", range = c("red", "green", "blue"))

The last line of code I found from this question <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/25496345/supply-a-vector-of-colours-to-be-used-in-ggvis-grouped-plot>, but it still doesn't tie a colour to a specific variable - it changes as I manipulate the text boxes.

