On 11/22/15, Brandon Hurr <brando...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Clint,
>
> A little more on this.
>
> Same setup as yours:
> mtcars %>%
> ggvis(~wt) %>%
>   filter(cyl %in% eval(input_checkboxgroup(c(4, 6, 8)))) %>%
>   layer_densities(fill := ~ cyl)
>
> Both your example and this one work as long as you uncheck a box before
> checking another, When you ask it to plot multiple densities at once, it
> blows up. I did ?layer_densities() and found this example:
>
> #this plots by group and colors them
> PlantGrowth %>% ggvis(~weight, fill = ~group) %>% group_by(group) %>%
>   layer_densities()
>
> #now we just need to filter it before grouping (I guess?)
> PlantGrowth %>%
> ggvis(~weight, fill = ~group) %>%
> filter(group %in% eval(input_checkboxgroup(c("ctrl", "trt1", "trt2")))) %>%
> group_by(group) %>%
> layer_densities()
> #seems to work. Note: I did not set a checked example so it loads up blank.
> Check and uncheck seems to work.
>
> HTH
>
> B
